\f0\fs24 \cf2 \cb3 \expnd0\expndtw0\kerning0
\outl0\strokewidth0 \strokec2 Because standard terminal pipelines (PTY/TTY) only transfer raw text characters rather than rich GUI MIME payloads, handling drag-and-drop and image pasting relies on two distinct mechanisms:\
\pard\pardeftab720\sa240\partightenfactor0

\f1\b \cf2 1. Drag and Drop (Files & Images)\
\pard\pardeftab720\sa240\partightenfactor0

\f0\b0 \cf2 Most modern terminal emulators (iTerm2, Ghostty, Kitty, WezTerm, Windows Terminal, Alacritty) handle drag-and-drop automatically at the emulator level.\
\pard\tx220\tx720\pardeftab720\li720\fi-720\partightenfactor0
\ls1\ilvl0
\f1\b \cf2 \kerning1\expnd0\expndtw0 \outl0\strokewidth0 {\listtext	\uc0\u8226 	}\expnd0\expndtw0\kerning0
\outl0\strokewidth0 \strokec2 How it works:
\f0\b0  When you drag a file or image from Finder, File Explorer, or your browser into the terminal window, the terminal emulator converts that OS event into standard input text containing the absolute file path (e.g., 
\f2\fs26 '/Users/username/Downloads/chart.png'
\f0\fs24 ).\cb1 \
\ls1\ilvl0
\f1\b \cb3 \kerning1\expnd0\expndtw0 \outl0\strokewidth0 {\listtext	\uc0\u8226 	}\expnd0\expndtw0\kerning0
\outl0\strokewidth0 \strokec2 What your TUI needs to do:
\f0\b0 \cb1 \
\pard\tx940\tx1440\pardeftab720\li1440\fi-1440\partightenfactor0
\ls1\ilvl1
\f1\b \cf2 \cb3 \kerning1\expnd0\expndtw0 \outl0\strokewidth0 {\listtext	1	}\expnd0\expndtw0\kerning0
\outl0\strokewidth0 \strokec2 Handle path parsing:
\f0\b0  Listen for input text, strip surrounding quotes (
\f2\fs26 '
\f0\fs24 , 
\f2\fs26 "
\f0\fs24 ) or backslash escapes (
\f2\fs26 \\ 
\f0\fs24 ), and check if the string represents an existing file on the filesystem using standard 
\f2\fs26 stat
\f0\fs24  / 
\f2\fs26 exists()
\f0\fs24  calls.\cb1 \
\ls1\ilvl1
\f1\b \cb3 \kerning1\expnd0\expndtw0 \outl0\strokewidth0 {\listtext	2	}\expnd0\expndtw0\kerning0
\outl0\strokewidth0 \strokec2 Bracketed Paste Mode:
\f0\b0  Ensure your TUI enables bracketed paste mode (
\f2\fs26 \\x1b[?2004h
\f0\fs24 ). This ensures that if a user drops multiple files or paths with spaces, the input arrives as a discrete paste event rather than being simulated keypress-by-keypress.\cb1 \
\pard\pardeftab720\sa240\partightenfactor0

\f1\b \cf2 \cb3 2. Copy/Paste Copied Image Data (Screenshots & Buffers)\
\pard\pardeftab720\sa240\partightenfactor0

\f0\b0 \cf2 When you take a screenshot to the clipboard (e.g., 
\f2\fs26 Cmd + Shift + Ctrl + 4
\f0\fs24  on macOS or 
\f2\fs26 Win + Shift + S
\f0\fs24  on Windows), there is no file path\'97the raw bitmap exists purely in system memory. Because terminals cannot receive binary image streams over stdin, 
\f1\b your TUI process must inspect the OS clipboard directly
\f0\b0 .\
\pard\pardeftab720\sa319\partightenfactor0

\f1\b \cf2 The Implementation Flow\
\pard\tx220\tx720\pardeftab720\li720\fi-720\partightenfactor0
\ls2\ilvl0
\f0\b0 \cf2 \kerning1\expnd0\expndtw0 \outl0\strokewidth0 {\listtext	1	}\expnd0\expndtw0\kerning0
\outl0\strokewidth0 \strokec2 User presses your paste shortcut (or your TUI intercepts 
\f2\fs26 Ctrl+V
\f0\fs24  / terminal paste event).\cb1 \
\ls2\ilvl0\cb3 \kerning1\expnd0\expndtw0 \outl0\strokewidth0 {\listtext	2	}\expnd0\expndtw0\kerning0
\outl0\strokewidth0 \strokec2 The TUI queries the OS clipboard API to see if an image MIME type is present (
\f2\fs26 image/png
\f0\fs24 , 
\f2\fs26 image/jpeg
\f0\fs24 ).\cb1 \
\ls2\ilvl0\cb3 \kerning1\expnd0\expndtw0 \outl0\strokewidth0 {\listtext	3	}\expnd0\expndtw0\kerning0
\outl0\strokewidth0 \strokec2 If image data exists:\cb1 \
\pard\tx940\tx1440\pardeftab720\li1440\fi-1440\partightenfactor0
\ls2\ilvl1\cf2 \cb3 \kerning1\expnd0\expndtw0 \outl0\strokewidth0 {\listtext	\uc0\u9702 	}\expnd0\expndtw0\kerning0
\outl0\strokewidth0 \strokec2 Extract the binary bytes.\cb1 \
\ls2\ilvl1\cb3 \kerning1\expnd0\expndtw0 \outl0\strokewidth0 {\listtext	\uc0\u9702 	}\expnd0\expndtw0\kerning0
\outl0\strokewidth0 \strokec2 Write them to a designated cache or temporary file (e.g., 
\f2\fs26 /tmp/agent_uploads/clip_20261003_120000.png
\f0\fs24 ).\cb1 \
\ls2\ilvl1\cb3 \kerning1\expnd0\expndtw0 \outl0\strokewidth0 {\listtext	\uc0\u9702 	}\expnd0\expndtw0\kerning0
\outl0\strokewidth0 \strokec2 Treat that path as the file input for your agent's multimodal payload.\cb1 \
\pard\tx220\tx720\pardeftab720\li720\fi-720\partightenfactor0
\ls2\ilvl0\cf2 \cb3 \kerning1\expnd0\expndtw0 \outl0\strokewidth0 {\listtext	4	}\expnd0\expndtw0\kerning0
\outl0\strokewidth0 \strokec2 If only text exists, proceed with standard text paste.\cb1 \
\pard\pardeftab720\sa319\partightenfactor0

